[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Read report by report, it is more than
one problem. The reports were merged on subject line alone
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and every one of them says "wrong date",
so nothing kept them apart.

<Callout kind="warn">
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October. The parser fix (<code>fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu
locales</code>) closes only the <code>parser</code> row. <code>hint</code> is won't fix: the
booking-v3 form is retired. <code>shift</code> is not fixed by either and stays open.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and these tenants write the day
  first, so day and month swap (2 March becomes 3 February). Any channel except a booking-v3 form.
  Fixed on 5 October.
- **`hint`**: tenants on booking-v3 get a form that prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, but
  the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. People type what the hint says and the
  date swaps. Only through the form, only on booking-v3. Fixing the parser does not fix this.
  Won't fix: booking-v3 is retired, so no new reports can come in this way.
- **`shift`**: the date moves by one day, not by a swap (Tuesday 12 May shows as Monday 11 May;
  one meeting is Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto; an invite arrives before the booking).
  That follows the reader's timezone, not the tenant's date order. The desk read these
  ([desk notes](https://github.com/tl-easygo/mega-s01e03/blob/main/src/lib/data/desk-notes.json))
  but filed them under `parser` by tenant.

## How the table counts

- One report per id: the ticket export repeats some reports across pages.
- `parser` or `hint` comes from the tenant's locale and booking form (`causes.ts`), not from
  intake's tag. Intake guesses from the reporter's browser and disagrees with the tenant on a
  share of these reports.
- A report the desk read as a one-day move counts as `shift`, and stays counted under the cause
  its tenant puts it in, as the desk counts. So the rows add up to more than the ticket.

## The same reports by cause

For comparison: the desk's own split, which has no row for `shift`.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## For triage

Matching on subject merges different bugs when every report uses the same words. A date report
needs two more questions before it is merged: does day swap with month, or move by one day? And
did it come through a booking form?

